name: Catalog import preserves existing metadata and reports partial work honestly
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sink_import.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
paste-file: @ART/merge-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 25 Saved catalog cannot be merged | merge-refused
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sink_import.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failed
ask: Does the failure explain that the prior catalog was preserved and name explicit replacement as a separate choice?
paste-file: @ART/replace-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Complete import is not claimed | partial-import
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sink_import.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
paste-file: @ART/partial-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · partial | partial-receipt
ask: Does the receipt keep the partial outcome, skipped-row warning and metadata-only boundary without claiming a completed Scan?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: partial-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: partial-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: partial-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: partial-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 partial | partial-40x12
keys: NPage NPage
live-snap: partial-detail-40x12
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sink_import.py @TMP_TARGET @ART warning
require-live-snap: 20 Complete import | partial-warning-40x12
ask: Are partial status and the warning reachable by paging across the six sizes, with readable recovery controls?
resize: 120x36
paste-file: @ART/failure-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Saved catalog cannot be merged | earlier-failure
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/partial-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · partial | recovered-partial
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sink_import.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain the partial import and earlier failure without another request, finding or Scan attempt?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
